{"availability":"available","full":"X-Square-Robot/X2Streaming-TTS","name":"X2Streaming-TTS","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":177,"forks":9,"created":"2026-08-12T09:47:09Z","updated":"2026-09-15T07:30:18Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://x-square-robot.github.io/X2Streaming-TTS/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:51.206Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:51.206Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:51.206Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T04:29:51.206Z","stars":177,"forks":9}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["X2Streaming-TTS + X2-NativeCursor — watch the 14-second speech-and-highlight recording, explore the scenarios, or connect your engine in the browser.","Illustrative scenarios for X2Streaming-TTS and X2-NativeCursor: start speaking as text arrives, maintain voice continuity across segments, synchronize text highlighting, use the playback clock to account for interruptions, and retain played content in dialogue history.","X2Streaming-TTS is the reference implementation of X2Streaming-TTS: Causal Token-Level Text-to-Speech from Streaming Text with Speech-State Inheritance. The paper introduces two mechanisms: causal commitment, which decides which text may be spoken and where a segment closes, and causal speech-state inheritance, which lets the next segment continue the voice of the previous one."],"features":["Strictly causal. An acoustic token depends only on text observed before it was","generated, previously generated acoustic tokens and inherited state.","Quality on par with offline decoding of the same weights. Lower recognition error","than the offline reference in 3 of 8 conditions; the largest degradation elsewhere is 0.62 percentage points.","Boundaries you cannot hear. Pitch discontinuity at segment boundaries drops to"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/X-Square-Robot/X2S